Governing law and NSW Trustee & Guardian duties
The NSW Trustee and Guardian Act 2009 (NSW) imposes clear duties on every person exercising functions in relation to a protected person. Section 39 requires that:
* the person’s welfare and interests be given paramount consideration;
* freedom of decision and freedom of action be restricted as little as possible;
* the person be encouraged, as far as possible, to live a normal life in the community;
* the person’s views be taken into consideration;
* the person be encouraged to be self-reliant in personal, domestic and financial affairs; and
* the person be protected from neglect, abuse and exploitation.
These are not aspirational statements. They are statutory principles. My objection is that decisions concerning my accommodation, finances, vehicle, support arrangements and independence must be measured against them.
