Australia’s international human-rights obligations
Australia is party to seven core international human-rights treaties: the ICCPR, ICESCR, CERD, CEDAW, CAT, CRC and CRPD. These obligations are relevant to the way a public authority exercises power over a person’s autonomy, welfare, financial security, accommodation, disability support and access to justice.
